course: dictionary
lesson: 6910
title: What is an oxide?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An oxide is a chemical made when an element joins with oxygen. The word always carries that clue: an oxide always has oxygen in it. «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide.»
explain: Iron oxide is the substance you know as rust. When iron meets oxygen and water over time, it forms iron oxide, which is why an old bike goes orange. The same kind of substance colours a whole planet red.
explain: Oxides are all around you. Carbon dioxide is made when things burn and when we breathe out, and zinc oxide is the white stuff in sun cream that helps protect your skin.
fact: An oxide is a chemical made when another element joins with oxygen.
fact: «Iron oxide» is rust.
fact: «Carbon dioxide» is made when things burn, and we breathe it out.
fact: «Zinc oxide» is used in sun cream.
fact: Water can be called hydrogen oxide, because hydrogen joins with oxygen in it.
exercise: «Mars looks red because its dust contains iron oxide.» What is iron oxide? | A gas we breathe out | A red planet | A type of sand from the beach | *A chemical made when iron joins with oxygen, which is rust
exercise: What is an oxide? | A metal that is very heavy | *A chemical made when another element joins with oxygen | A rock found on the Moon | A gas that is always blue
exercise: Which of these is an oxide? | Silver | Gold | Iron wire | *Carbon dioxide
test: Rust is iron oxide. What is rust made from? | Salt | *Iron joining with oxygen | Carbon | Zinc
test: «Zinc oxide» is in sun cream. Why is it used on skin? | To make the cream smell nice | To freeze the skin | To make skin glow green | *To help protect skin from the Sun
exam: Which word means a chemical made when an element joins with oxygen? | Oxygen | Metal | Element | *Oxide
